LOCAL PATCH (not submitted anywhere): watchdog: sp805 — restart with a non-zero load

HiSilicon Hi3798CV200 SP805 never expires from WDTLOAD = 0, so the restart handler hung reboot
forever. Use 0x100, as the vendor kernel does.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/sp805_wdt.c	2026-10-11 18:27:30
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sp805_wdt.c	2026-10-11 18:27:30
@@ -140,7 +140,13 @@
 
 	writel_relaxed(UNLOCK, wdt->base + WDTLOCK);
 	writel_relaxed(0, wdt->base + WDTCONTROL);
-	writel_relaxed(0, wdt->base + WDTLOAD);
+	/*
+	 * LOCAL (HiMedia Q10 Pro / Hi3798CV200): HiSilicon's SP805 never expires from a LOAD of 0
+	 * — measured 2026-10-11: sysrq-b sat in this handler until an unrelated arming fired 190 s
+	 * later. The vendor kernel restarts with LOAD = 0x100 (mach-hi3798cv2x/core.c), i.e. two
+	 * expiries of 256 ticks; do the same.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(0x100, wdt->base + WDTLOAD);
 	writel_relaxed(INT_ENABLE | RESET_ENABLE, wdt->base + WDTCONTROL);
 
 	/* Flush posted writes. */
